      "id": "secure-domestic-travel-tsa-mobile-drivers-license-at-airport-checkpoints-IyxXZl",
      "sector": "mobility",
      "title": "USA Secure Domestic Travel: TSA Mobile Driver's License at Airport Checkpoints",
      "summary": "TSA enables domestic travelers to present a mobile driver's license (mDL) instead of a physical ID for identity verification at airport security checkpoints. Travelers get a contactless experience that shares only 6 data fields; TSA gets stronger assurance that the document is real and faster processing; issuing states lay the groundwork for a broader Digital ID ecosystem.\n\nThe use case is live. In May 2026, mDLs were presented at 271 airports, with 45,800 transactions that month. Monthly volume grew from 22,000 in March 2025 to 46,000 in May 2026. Twenty-one states and territories issue accepted credentials, presented through 13 wallet applications: Apple Wallet, Google Wallet, Samsung Wallet, and 10 state-issued apps. Each app has passed DHS/TSA requirements so the Digital ID retains REAL ID standards.\n\nHaving a lead, example Use Case for mDL acceptance has been essential to the adoption of Mobile Driver’s License in the United States.  TSA has set the example for participation by Relying Parties that accept mDL and created a level of momentum of the ecosystem that has been difficult to obtain with solely commercial Relying Parties.  Acceptance at TSA has become core requirements",
